From 6228e1a7484621089998a283fe24276985278999 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:39:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(tools): the tool editor's to-scale preview follows
 the drawn profile

The middle "what verify would collide" preview read the tool_body_ui
draft, re-mirrored from the world only inside the Body tab's section.
With the Profile tab showing it drew the plain cylinder after Apply
profile and after reload, and kept the drawn envelope after Cmd+Z. The
preview's envelope() now re-syncs the draft first (a no-op unless the
world's body changed), so it follows Apply, undo and reload whichever
tab shows.

Also: an Apply profile refusal stayed on screen after the outline was
corrected. The refused outline is remembered; once the draft moves off
it and validates, that refusal retires (banner and status line). A
refusal of the very outline still on screen stands.

Pinned by egui_app::tests::tool_profile::
the_to_scale_preview_follows_the_profile_without_the_body_tab and
a_profile_refusal_retires_when_the_outline_validates (both fail before
the fix).

Refs #93

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
